== 2.7 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The accounting equation is],
  [assets = capital − liabilities],
  [liabilities = assets + capital],
  [capital = assets + liabilities],
  [assets = liabilities + capital]
)

#mcq(2, [A firm has assets of ₦500,000 and liabilities of ₦180,000. Its capital is],
  [₦500,000],
  [₦680,000],
  [₦180,000],
  [₦320,000]
)

#mcq(3, [The expanded accounting equation is],
  [assets = liabilities + capital + drawings − profit],
  [capital = assets + profit − liabilities],
  [assets = liabilities + capital + profit − drawings],
  [assets + profit = liabilities + capital]
)

#mcq(4, [Goods bought on credit will],
  [increase assets and increase liabilities],
  [decrease capital],
  [increase assets only],
  [increase liabilities only]
)

#mcq(5, [Furniture bought for cash will],
  [increase total assets],
  [decrease total assets],
  [increase capital],
  [leave total assets unchanged]
)

#mcq(6, [Which transaction increases capital?],
  [drawings by the owner],
  [a profit for the year],
  [payment of a creditor],
  [purchase of stock for cash]
)

#mcq(7, [Which transaction reduces capital?],
  [a cash sale at a profit],
  [drawings by the owner],
  [goods bought on credit],
  [a loan received]
)

#mcq(8, [A debit entry increases],
  [liabilities, income and capital],
  [expenses, assets and drawings],
  [income and capital],
  [liabilities and expenses]
)

#mcq(9, [A credit entry increases],
  [assets and expenses],
  [drawings],
  [purchases],
  [liabilities, income and capital]
)

#mcq(10, [Goods returned by a customer are recorded as],
  [debit sales, credit cash],
  [debit returns inwards, credit the debtor],
  [debit the debtor, credit returns inwards],
  [debit purchases, credit the debtor]
)

#mcq(11, [Goods returned to a supplier are recorded as],
  [debit creditor, credit returns outwards],
  [debit creditor, credit purchases],
  [debit purchases, credit creditor],
  [debit returns outwards, credit creditor]
)

#mcq(12, [Discount allowed to a customer is],
  [credited as income],
  [ignored],
  [debited as an expense],
  [debited to capital]
)

#mcq(13, [Discount received from a supplier is],
  [a liability],
  [a reduction of stock],
  [an expense],
  [income]
)

#mcq(14, [A bad debt written off is recorded as],
  [debit the debtor, credit bad debts],
  [debit sales, credit bad debts],
  [debit bad debts, credit the debtor],
  [debit cash, credit the debtor]
)

#mcq(15, [A cash sale is recorded as],
  [debit cash, credit sales],
  [debit sales, credit cash],
  [debit purchases, credit cash],
  [debit debtor, credit sales]
)

#mcq(16, [Payment to a creditor is recorded as],
  [debit purchases, credit cash],
  [debit creditor, credit purchases],
  [debit creditor, credit cash],
  [debit cash, credit creditor]
)

#mcq(17, [Receipt from a debtor is recorded as],
  [debit cash, credit sales],
  [debit cash, credit debtor],
  [debit debtor, credit cash],
  [debit sales, credit debtor]
)

#mcq(18, [Cash withdrawn by the owner is recorded as],
  [debit expenses, credit cash],
  [debit drawings, credit cash],
  [debit capital, credit cash],
  [debit cash, credit drawings]
)

#mcq(19, [Capital introduced in cash is recorded as],
  [debit cash, credit capital],
  [debit drawings, credit cash],
  [debit cash, credit sales],
  [debit capital, credit cash]
)

#mcq(20, [A bank loan received is recorded as],
  [debit cash, credit capital],
  [debit cash, credit loan],
  [debit loan, credit cash],
  [debit capital, credit loan]
)

#mcq(21, [A motor van bought on credit is recorded as],
  [debit motor van, credit creditor],
  [debit creditor, credit motor van],
  [debit motor expenses, credit creditor],
  [debit purchases, credit cash]
)

#mcq(22, [Depreciation for the year is recorded as],
  [debit accumulated depreciation, credit depreciation expense],
  [debit depreciation expense, credit accumulated depreciation],
  [debit the asset, credit cash],
  [debit capital, credit the asset]
)

#mcq(23, [An accrued expense is recorded as],
  [debit prepayment, credit expense],
  [debit expense, credit accrual],
  [debit cash, credit expense],
  [debit accrual, credit expense]
)

#mcq(24, [A prepayment is recorded as],
  [debit accrual, credit expense],
  [debit expense, credit prepayment],
  [debit prepayment, credit expense],
  [debit cash, credit prepayment]
)

#mcq(25, [When an account is balanced off, the balance is written],
  [on the smaller side],
  [on the larger side],
  [in the trial balance only],
  [outside the account]
)

#mcq(26, [A debit balance brought down is entered on the],
  [debit side of the next period],
  [trial balance only],
  [same side as the closing balance],
  [credit side of the next period]
)

#mcq(27, [The main purpose of a trial balance is to],
  [check that total debits equal total credits],
  [compute profit],
  [prove that no errors were made],
  [value the stock]
)

#mcq(28, [Which account normally has a debit balance?],
  [sales],
  [rent],
  [capital],
  [creditors]
)

#mcq(29, [Which account normally has a credit balance?],
  [drawings],
  [returns inwards],
  [purchases],
  [provision for doubtful debts]
)

#mcq(30, [Assets are ₦850,000 and liabilities ₦320,000. Capital is],
  [₦320,000],
  [₦1,170,000],
  [₦530,000],
  [₦850,000]
)

#mcq(31, [Closing capital is ₦530,000, profit ₦70,000 and drawings ₦30,000. Opening capital was],
  [₦570,000],
  [₦630,000],
  [₦490,000],
  [₦430,000]
)

#mcq(32, [Paying a creditor by cheque will],
  [increase liabilities],
  [reduce assets only],
  [increase capital],
  [reduce assets and reduce liabilities]
)

#mcq(33, [A credit sale at a profit will],
  [increase liabilities],
  [reduce capital],
  [increase assets and increase capital],
  [increase assets only]
)

#mcq(34, [A debit balance on the cash account means],
  [cash is held by the firm],
  [the account has not been balanced],
  [cash is owed by the firm],
  [an overdraft exists]
)

#mcq(35, [Which transaction leaves total assets unchanged?],
  [cash introduced by the owner],
  [a loan received],
  [stock bought for cash],
  [goods bought on credit]
)

#mcq(36, [The double entry for a purchase return is],
  [debit creditor, credit returns outwards],
  [debit cash, credit purchases],
  [debit purchases, credit creditor],
  [debit returns outwards, credit creditor]
)

#mcq(37, [The accounting equation stays in balance because],
  [cash is always available],
  [profits are always positive],
  [every transaction has two effects of equal amount],
  [assets are always equal to cash]
)

#mcq(38, [Opening capital ₦300,000; capital introduced ₦100,000; drawings ₦40,000; closing capital ₦420,000. Profit was],
  [₦60,000],
  [₦80,000],
  [₦100,000],
  [₦160,000]
)

#mcq(39, [Which statement about capital is correct?],
  [it is what the business owes its owner],
  [it is an asset of the business],
  [it is a liability to outsiders],
  [it is the same as cash]
)

#mcq(40, [If a transaction is recorded on one side only, the accounting equation will],
  [still balance],
  [be unaffected],
  [no longer balance],
  [double]
)

